<title>EGYPT: Eli Lilly &amp; Co to invest $22 mln in Egypt.</title>
<headline>Eli Lilly &amp; Co to invest $22 mln in Egypt.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. firm Eli Lilly and Company will build a pharmaceuticals plant in Egypt for a total investment of $22 million, U.S. Commerce Secretary Mickey Kantor said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He told reporters at the Middle East and North Africa economic conference in Cairo the plant would be operational by 1998.</p>
<p>The plant will make products such as antibiotics and human insulin for local and foreign markets, he added.</p>
<p>($1=3.4 pounds)</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom+ 20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
